==Trivia==
*The word "''Bomb''" comes from the Greek "''βόμβος''" (''bómbos)'', meaning booming or buzzing, referring to the sound that bombs do when they explode. Bombs were first invented in China during the ninth century. Initialy, they were made with ceramic material along with gunpowder, however, they were later changed to cast-iron shells with the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunder_crash_bomb Thunder crash bomb] during the twelve century.
*The Bomb Tower is 1 of 15 [[cards]] associated with [[Skeletons]], with the others being [[Bomber]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Tombstone]], [[Guards]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Super Witch]], [[Graveyard]], [[Skeleton King]], and of course, Skeletons.
*The Bomb Tower is the only [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] that inspired a building in Clash of Clans.
*Among all buildings with area damage, the Bomb Tower has the smallest area damage radius of all buildings, with a radius of 1.5 tiles.
*The Cannon is one of the first building cards to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the [[Cannon]], [[Goblin Hut]], Tombstone, [[Inferno Tower]], and [[Barbarian Hut]].
*Though not the first [[cards]] to receive balance changes, the Bomb Tower is one of the first {{Rarity|Rare}} cards to ever receive balance changes since the [[Version History#February 2016 Update (2/2/2016)|February 2016 Update]], the others are the [[Wizard]], Inferno Tower, Barbarian Hut, and [[Elixir Collector]].
*The Bomb Tower is the only building that has been featured with a [[Buff#Knockback Attack|Knockback Attack]] [[buff]].
*The Bomb Tower is 1 of 23 cards that has had its [[Elixir]] cost changed, the others being Bomber, [[Fire Spirit]], [[Royal Recruits]], Cannon, [[Mortar]], [[Musketeer]], [[Three Musketeers]], [[Heal]], Goblin Hut, Barbarian Hut, [[Furnace]], Elixir Collector, Skeleton Army, [[P.E.K.K.A.]], Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], [[Bowler]], [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Rage]], [[Fisherman]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Bomb Tower is unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 20 cards that is unavailable in [[Mirror]] mode, the others being [[Minions]], Cannon, Mortar, [[Tesla]], Goblin Hut, Tombstone, Inferno Tower, Barbarian Hut, Furnace, Elixir Collector, [[Freeze]], [[Clone]], [[X-Bow]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Little Prince]], and the Monk.
**It is unavailable in [[Global Spell|The Floor is Healing]] sub-[[:Category:Modes|mode]] of the Global Spell game mode, much like other building cards, as well as the [[Cannon Cart]].
*The Bomb Tower was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/cmBlEI-aDoo?si=UoD1Sit2YvQR19xs Clash Royale League 2019 Tournament], by a player called Surgical Goblin.
*There used to be a glitch where if a Bomb Tower was directly in front of the [[King's Tower]] and was hit by [[The Log]], the Bomb Tower would extend The Log's effective range, causing it to activate the King's Tower.
*In [[Touchdown]], if a Bomb Tower is still on the [[Arenas|Arena]] after a touchdown has been scored, it will have its dropped bomb cleared.
* Before the Bomb Tower's card release, the Bomb Tower's cost was decreased to 5 Elixir (from 6 Elixir), its hitpoints were increased by 12.5%, its damage was decreased by 16%, and its attack time interval was decreased to 1.8 seconds (from 1.9 seconds).

